/// Static behavioral API documentation for the Honey Do's backend.
///
/// This mixin exposes a single read-only `getApiDoc` query. The document is a
/// static Markdown literal authored from the current backend source; it reads
/// no actor state and never changes at runtime.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend's behavioral API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Honey Do's Backend API\n\nHoney Do's is a handyman job-request service. Guests submit job requests\nwithout an account and track them with a public reference code. An\nadministrator signs in to quote, schedule, and progress those jobs, manage the\nbee crew, assign bees to jobs, enroll customers in the monthly package, and\nreview each customer's visit history. Every new request also alerts the owner\nimmediately by email and by SMS.\n\nThe backend also keeps a permanent customer database. Every submitted request\nresolves to a customer record (matched on normalized email first, then\nnormalized phone) so returning customers are recognized instead of duplicated.\nAdministrators manage customers, notes, statuses, messages and dashboard\nnotifications through the customer, notification and message endpoints below.\n\nThe service-management workflow is: REQUEST -> QUOTE (with automatic discounts)\n-> CUSTOMER APPROVAL -> AUTOMATIC DEPOSIT -> PAYMENT -> ADMIN VERIFICATION ->\nCONFIRMED CALENDAR APPOINTMENT -> JOB -> REMAINING BALANCE -> COMPLETED. A\nrequested date/time is never a confirmed booking until the required deposit has\nbeen submitted and verified by the owner.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- **Guest endpoints** (`submitRequest`, `getRequestByReference`, `acceptQuote`,\n  `getQuoteByReference`, `declineQuoteByReference`,\n  `createDepositCheckoutSession`, `confirmDepositPayment`, `recordDeposit`,\n  `submitDeposit`, `getPaymentSummary`, `confirmAppointment`, `submitReview`,\n  `getVisitHistory`, `postCustomerMessage`, `getCustomerMessages`) require no\n  sign-in. They are callable by anonymous and signed-in callers alike. A\n  customer can only ever read or write their own thread, because the customer is\n  resolved from the job reference code they already hold.\n- **Admin endpoints** require a signed-in caller whose role is `#admin`. Every\n  admin endpoint traps with `Unauthorized: Only admins can perform this action`\n  for an anonymous caller or a signed-in caller without the admin role. This\n  covers `listRequests`, `getRequest`, `setQuote`, `editQuote`, `sendQuote`,\n  `approveQuote`, `declineQuote`, `convertQuoteToJob`, `scheduleAppointment`,\n  `advanceStatus`, `cancelJob`, `getDashboardStats`, `createBee`, `updateBee`,\n  `listBees`, `assignBeeToJob`, `setPackageEnrollment`,\n  `getCustomerVisitHistory`, `createJobForCustomer`, `getOwnerAlertEmail`,\n  `setOwnerAlertEmail`, `getOwnerAlertPhone`, `setOwnerAlertPhone`,\n  `getTwilioConfigStatus`, `setTwilioCredentials`, `sendTestAlert`,\n  `getFrontendOrigin`, `setFrontendOrigin`, `listCustomers`, `searchCustomers`,\n  `getCustomer`, `getCustomerProfile`, `createCustomer`, `updateCustomer`,\n  `addCustomerNote`, `setCustomerStatus`, `archiveCustomer`, `restoreCustomer`,\n  `exportCustomersCsv`, `listNotifications`, `getUnreadNotificationCount`,\n  `markNotificationRead`, `markAllNotificationsRead`, `listCustomerMessages`,\n  `postAdminMessage`, `listDiscounts`, `createDiscount`, `updateDiscount`,\n  `setDiscountActive`, `deleteDiscount`, `getSettings`, `setTaxSetting`,\n  `setDepositSetting`, `setPaymentSettings`, `setQuoteSettings`,\n  `setBusinessSettings`, `setAdminSettings`, `verifyDeposit`, `rejectDeposit`,\n  `listPaymentHistory`, `getPaymentHistoryForJob`, `listJobRecords`,\n  `getJobRecord`, `createJobRecord`, `advanceJobRecord`, `completeJobRecord`,\n  `cancelJobRecord`, `recordFinalPayment`, `sendAppointmentReminder`.\n- **Identity derivation.** The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity\n  derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when\n  available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization\n  derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\n  user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- **Registration prerequisite.** Access control is initialized on first use.\n  A direct API caller must register before any role-guarded call: call\n  `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller. The first initializer\n  receives the `#admin` role; subsequent callers receive the default role and\n  must be promoted by an admin. An unregistered or anonymous caller receives the\n  trap `Unauthorized: Only admins can perform this action` on every guarded\n  endpoint, guarded queries included. A caller can be unregistered while\n  assuming the app already knows it: registration happens only when a caller\n  signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is\n  unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller\n  derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the\n  frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Money** is in whole US cents (`Nat`). `$250.00` is `25000`.\n- **Timestamps** are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch\n  (`Time.now()`). A `?Timestamp` is `null` when unset.\n- **Identifiers** are `Nat` counters (`JobId`, `CustomerId`, `DiscountId`,\n  `JobRecordId`, `PaymentId`, `BeeId`, `NotificationId`, `MessageId`).\n- **Reference codes** are public `Text` values of the form `HD-<digits>`.\n- **Photo ids** are `Text` object-storage keys.\n- **Variants** cross the Candid boundary as tagged values; generated Motoko\n  bindings use `__kind__` discriminants.\n- **Result** values are `{ #ok : T; #err : E }`; branch on the tag, never on a\n  string.\n\n## Pricing, discounts and the deposit\n\n- A quote's pricing is computed automatically by the pricing engine. The admin\n  supplies line items, labor and materials charges; the backend derives the\n  original subtotal, the applicable discount, the adjusted subtotal, tax (when\n  enabled), the final total, the deposit and the remaining balance.\n- Discount rules are admin-managed (`createDiscount`, `updateDiscount`,\n  `setDiscountActive`, `deleteDiscount`). A rule is a percentage or a fixed\n  amount, with an active flag, an optional start/end window, an eligibility\n  rule (`#all`, `#ownParts`, `#returningCustomer`), an optional minimum purchase\n  and an optional maximum discount. Expired, inactive or ineligible rules are\n  never applied. The pricing breakdown carries a `discount.reason` explaining\n  why a discount was or was not applied.\n- The deposit is exactly the configured percentage of the final quote total\n  after discounts and adjustments (10% by default). The customer never\n  calculates it. `depositAmount` and `remainingBalance` always add up to\n  `finalTotal`.\n- `getPaymentSummary(referenceCode)` is the customer payment page: original\n  amount, discount, final quote, deposit required, remaining balance, accepted\n  payment methods with the owner's handles, and the current deposit and\n  appointment state.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A request starts `#requested`. Setting a quote moves it to `#quoted`; an\n  approved quote converted to a job moves it to `#scheduled`; `advanceStatus`\n  walks `#scheduled -> #inProgress -> #completed`. `#cancelled` is terminal.\n- A deposit starts `#pending`, becomes `#submitted` when the customer reports\n  paying, and ends `#verified` (owner confirmed) or `#rejected` (owner did not\n  receive it, so the customer may resubmit).\n- A job record starts `#scheduled` and advances `#scheduled -> #inProgress ->\n  #completed`; `#cancelled` is terminal.\n- Poll `getRequestByReference` / `getPaymentSummary` for a customer's state and\n  `listRequests` / `listJobRecords` / `listPaymentHistory` for the admin view.\n  There is no push channel; the frontend polls and the owner alert is raised\n  in-app.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `submitRequest` is **not idempotent**: each call creates a new request with a\n  new reference code. Do not retry blindly.\n- `setQuote` / `editQuote` replace the quote and recompute pricing; retrying is\n  safe but recomputes from the current settings.\n- `sendQuote` emails the customer and is **not** idempotent in effect: a retry\n  sends another email. It returns the per-channel email outcome and the updated\n  view.\n- `submitDeposit` sets the deposit to `#submitted`; `verifyDeposit` and\n  `rejectDeposit` are idempotent in state but raise a notification each call.\n- `recordFinalPayment` updates the permanent payment-history entry; retrying\n  with the same amount overwrites the final payment rather than adding to it.\n- `createJobRecord` returns the existing job when one already exists for the\n  request, so it is safe to retry.\n- `createCustomer` / `createDiscount` / `createBee` allocate a new id per call;\n  retrying creates a duplicate.\n\n## Errors, traps and limits\n\n- Admin endpoints trap (not `#err`) on an unauthorized caller. Guest endpoints\n  return `#err` variants (`JobError`, `QuoteError`, `PaymentError`,\n  `MessageError`) for expected failures such as `#notFound` or `#invalidState`.\n- `acceptQuote` rejects an expired quote with `#invalidState`; an expired quote\n  cannot be accepted.\n- `verifyDeposit` requires a `#submitted` deposit; `rejectDeposit` likewise.\n- `sendAppointmentReminder` returns `#invalidState` when appointment reminders\n  are turned off in settings or no appointment is scheduled.\n- Email and SMS sends are best-effort: a delivery failure is reported in the\n  result and never aborts the state change.\n\n## Non-obvious gotchas\n\n- A requested date/time is not a confirmed booking until the deposit is\n  verified; `appointmentConfirmed` stays false until then.\n- The deposit is computed from the final total after discounts and tax, not from\n  the raw subtotal.\n- `getPaymentSummary` and `getQuoteByReference` are guest-readable by reference\n  code; treat the reference code as the customer's bearer credential.\n- Payment methods are the owner's own supplied handles (PayPal, Cash App,\n  Venmo, Chime); the app never invents or changes them. Deposit verification is\n  manual until a real payment-provider integration exists.\n";
  };
};
